      <div type="clause" n="43.1">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Ine">Ine</ref> 43.1</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="43.1" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="108" ed="#liebermann"/>Gif mon afelle<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#Ine_43-1.lnote.oe.8-2"/> on wuda wel<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#Ine_43-1.lnote.oe.9-2"/> monega<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#Ine_43-1.lnote.oe.10-3"/> treowa, ⁊ wyrð eft<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#Ine_43-1.lnote.oe.11-3"/> undierne, forgielde<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#Ine_43-1.lnote.oe.12-3"/> III treowu ælc mid XXX<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#Ine_43-1.lnote.oe.13-2"/> scill.; ne ðearf he hiora<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="14" target="#Ine_43-1.lnote.oe.14"/> má geldan<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="15" target="#Ine_43-1.lnote.oe.15"/>, wære hiora<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="16" target="#Ine_43-1.lnote.oe.16"/> swa fela swa hiora wære: forþon<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="17" target="#Ine_43-1.lnote.oe.17"/> sio ǽsc bið melda, nalles<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="18" target="#Ine_43-1.lnote.oe.18"/> ðeof.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="43.1" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="108" ed="#liebermann"/>Gif mon<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#Ine_43-1.lnote.oe.7"/> afylle<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#Ine_43-1.lnote.oe.8"/> on wuda wel monige<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#Ine_43-1.lnote.oe.7"/> treowa<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#Ine_43-1.lnote.oe.9"/>, ⁊ wyrð eft undyrne<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Ine_43-1.lnote.oe.5"/>, forgilde ðreo<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#Ine_43-1.lnote.oe.10-2"/> treowa<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#Ine_43-1.lnote.oe.9"/> ælc mid XXX scll'; ne þearf he nan má gildon<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#Ine_43-1.lnote.oe.7"/>, wære heora<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#Ine_43-1.lnote.oe.10-2"/> swa fela<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#Ine_43-1.lnote.oe.11-2"/> swa heora<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#Ine_43-1.lnote.oe.10-2"/> wære: forðon seo æx bið melda, nalæs<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#Ine_43-1.lnote.oe.12-2"/> ðeof.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="43.1" corresp="#wit-b-no-prol"><pb n="108" ed="#liebermann"/>Gyf mon afylle on wuda well<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Ine_43-1.lnote.oe.2"/> manega treowe, ⁊ wurð þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> eft undyrne, forgylde ðreo tréowa ælc mid ðrittig scill'; ne ðearf he heora ma gyldan, wære heora swa feola swa heora wære: forðan seo eax bið melda, nalæs ðeof.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="43.1" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="109" ed="#liebermann"/>Si quis in nemore multa ligna ceciderit, et postea compareat, soluat tria ligna unumquodque triginta sol.; nec<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#Ine_43-1.lnote.oe.10"/> amplius cogitur per legem soluere, quotquot fuerint, quia securis<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#Ine_43-1.lnote.oe.11"/> acclamatrix potius<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#Ine_43-1.lnote.oe.12"/> est, non<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#Ine_43-1.lnote.oe.13"/> fur.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="50" ed="#attenborough"/>Gif mon afelle<ptr type="editorNote" n="10" target="#Ine_43-1.attnote.fn.10"/> on wuda wel monega treowa, ⁊ wyrð eft<ptr type="editorNote" n="11" target="#Ine_43-1.attnote.fn.11"/> undierne, forgielde III treowu ælc mid XXX scill.; ne ðearf he hiora má geldan<ptr type="editorNote" n="12" target="#Ine_43-1.attnote.fn.12"/>, wære hiora swa fela swa hiora wære; forþon sio ǽsc<ptr type="editorNote" n="13" target="#Ine_43-1.attnote.fn.13"/> bið melda, nalles ðeof.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="44.1" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="408" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>Gif mon afelle on wuda wel monega treowa ⁊ wyrð eft undierne, forgielde III treowu ælc mid XXX sciƚƚ. Ne ðearf he hiora má geldan, wære hiora swa fela swa hiora wære, forþon sio ǽsc bið melda, nalles ðeof.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="109" ed="#liebermann"/>Wenn jemand im Walde gar viele Bäume fällt, und es wird späterhin bekannt, entgelte er [nur<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Ine_43-1.lnote.de.1"/>] 3 Bäume jeden mit 30<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Ine_43-1.lnote.de.2"/> Schill.; ihrer mehr braucht er<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Ine_43-1.lnote.de.3"/> nicht zu zahlen, wären ihrer [auch<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Ine_43-1.lnote.de.4"/>] so viele wie ihrer wären: denn die Axt<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Ine_43-1.lnote.de.5"/> ist ein Anzeiger<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Ine_43-1.lnote.de.6"/>, nicht ein Dieb.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">If someone fells a great many trees in the wood, and it becomes known later, let him pay for [only] 3 trees, each with 30 shillings; he need not pay for more of them, however many of them there might be: for the axe is an informer, not a thief.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="51" ed="#attenborough"/>If anyone fells a large number of trees in a wood, and it afterwards becomes known, he shall pay 30 shillings for each of three trees. He need not pay for more, however many there may be, because the axe is an informer and not a thief.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="404" ed="#whitelock"/>If anyone fells in the wood quite a number of trees, and it afterwards becomes known, he is to pay for three trees at 30 shillings each; he need not pay for more of them however many they were, for the axe is an informer, not a thief.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="409" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>If a man fells many trees in the forest, and it afterwards is revealed, let him make restitution for three trees each with 30 shillings. He need not make restitution for more no matter how many there were, because the axe is an informant but not a thief.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="409"><label>contrast</label> <ref target="clause:Af_12">Af 12</ref> <quote>Contrast with Alfred §14, which sets an equal fine for felling or burning another's wood.</quote></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="278"><label>contradicts</label> <ref target="clause:Af_12">Af 12</ref> <quote>there are differences in the sums levied for ... felling another's trees (n. 72: Af 12, Ine 43:1)</quote></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="309"><label>contrast</label> <ref target="clause:Af_12">Af 12</ref> <quote>Ine §44.1 requires the first three trees felled to be recompensed with 30 shillings each</quote></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_43-1.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">108</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">später auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">later on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_43-1.lnote.oe.10" n="10" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">109</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">neque <hi rend="italic">M Hk Br</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">neque M Hk Br</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_43-1.lnote.oe.11" n="11" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">109</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ignis fur est <hi rend="italic">statt</hi> securis — fur <hi rend="italic">Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ignis fur est instead of securis — fur Lond</seg></note>
