        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_43-1.lnote.oe.15" n="15" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">108</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">gyl. <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">gyl. Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_43-1.lnote.oe.16" n="16" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">108</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">heora s. feola s. heora <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">heora s. feola s. heora Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_43-1.lnote.oe.17" n="17" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">108</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-þan seo eax <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-þan seo eax Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_43-1.lnote.oe.18" n="18" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">108</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">na læs <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">na læs Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_43-1.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">76</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Für den vierten und jeden weiteren Baum wird Entgelt absorbiert; Schreuer <hi rend="italic">Verbrechenskonk.</hi> 37. 115</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">For the fourth and every further tree the payment is absorbed; Schreuer <hi rend="italic">Verbrechenskonk.</hi> 37. 115</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_43-1.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">76</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Über Schätzung des Holzes auch in Wäldern, die noch Gemeinheit, <hi rend="italic">s.</hi> Vinogradoff <hi rend="italic">Growth</hi> 168. Ine meint wohl nicht Busse (<hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 6f.), denn der Betrag ist als Sachwert viel zu hoch laut Af 12. <hi rend="italic">Forgieldan</hi> bezeichnet Strafentgelt zahlen an den Richter auch Ine 36 (auch II As 1, 1; 4).</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">On the valuation of timber also in woods that are still common land, <hi rend="italic">see</hi> Vinogradoff <hi rend="italic">Growth</hi> 168. Ine probably does not mean compensation (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 6f.), for the amount is far too high as the value of the object, according to Af 12. <hi rend="italic">Forgieldan</hi> denotes the payment of a penal sum to the judge also in Ine 36 (also II As 1, 1; 4).</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_43-1.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">76</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Der Einschub Q’s <hi rend="italic">per legem</hi> bedeutet bei diesem Verf. ‘gemäss [Angelsächs.] Gesetzbuch (<hi rend="italic">s. Wb: lex</hi> 4), im Ggs. zu heutigem [weit härteren] Forstrecht’. Vielleicht dachte er hierbei schon an sein künftiges Rechtsbuch Hn über geltendes Recht</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Q’s insertion <hi rend="italic">per legem</hi> means, in this author, ‘according to the [Anglo-Saxon] law-book (<hi rend="italic">see Wb: lex</hi> 4), in contrast to present-day [far harsher] forest law’. Perhaps in this he was already thinking of his future law-book Hn on the law in force</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_43-1.lnote.de.4" n="4" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">76</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">‘es mögen so viel sein als es wollen’ Schmid freier</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">‘be they as many as they will’ Schmid, more freely</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_43-1.lnote.de.5" n="5" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">76</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Anzeiger; Anzeige 3. 10</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Anzeiger; Anzeige 3. 10</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_43-1.lnote.de.6" n="6" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">76</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Anzeiger; Anzeige 3. 10</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Anzeiger; Anzeige 3. 10</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Ine_43-1.attnote.fn.10" n="10" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">50</biblScope></bibl><label>afelle</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">afylleð</hi>. H. <hi rend="italic">afylle</hi>. B.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Ine_43-1.attnote.fn.11" n="11" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">50</biblScope></bibl><label>eft</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">wurð þæt eft</hi>. B.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Ine_43-1.attnote.fn.12" n="12" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">50</biblScope></bibl><label>geldan</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">he nan ma gildon</hi>. H.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Ine_43-1.attnote.fn.13" n="13" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">50</biblScope></bibl><label>ǽsc</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">seo æx</hi>. H. <hi rend="italic">seo eax</hi>. B.</seg></note>
